cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or report, cite it as below."
title: "Magnesium Supplementation: An Independent Evidence Review and Product Database"
abstract: >-
  A structured review of magnesium forms, elemental content, absorption,
  bioavailability and gastrointestinal effects, covering sleep, muscle function,
  cramps, recovery, anxiety, migraine, cardiovascular health and cognition. Includes
  deficiency and status testing, dosing and upper limits, kidney and toxicity risks,
  drug interactions, product quality and certification, cost per elemental dose, and
  a reproducible validation pipeline.
